Package: zapretgui
Version: @VERSION@
Section: net
Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: Zapret <noreply@zapret.moe>
Depends: libc6 (>= 2.38), nftables, libluajit-5.1-2, zlib1g, libnetfilter-queue1, libnfnetlink0, libmnl0, libcap2, libxcb-cursor0, libxkbcommon-x11-0, libegl1, libgl1, libfontconfig1, libdbus-1-3, libx11-6, libx11-xcb1, libxcb1, libxcb-glx0, libxcb-icccm4, libxcb-image0, libxcb-keysyms1, libxcb-randr0, libxcb-render0, libxcb-render-util0, libxcb-shape0, libxcb-shm0, libxcb-sync1, libxcb-util1, libxcb-xfixes0, libxcb-xkb1, libxkbcommon0, libwayland-client0, libwayland-cursor0, libglib2.0-0t64
Recommends: pkexec | policykit-1, polkitd | policykit-1, libnotify-bin, xdg-utils
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Homepage: https://wiki.zapret.moe/
Description: Zapret: bypass of network blocks with a window
 Presets, tray icon, DNS settings and checks on top of zapret2 (nfqws2).
 The window runs as the normal user; a small root service (zapretgui-helper)
 owns the firewall table "inet zapretgui" and the engine.
